Cross builds for QNX: generate the VM for a POSIX target, not OS_OTHER.

When HOST_SYS != TARGET_SYS, src/Makefile compiles buildvm with a LUAJIT_OS
matching the target -- but only for Windows, Linux, Darwin and iOS.  Any other
TARGET_SYS gets LUAJIT_OS_OTHER.  The target's own sources see __QNX__ and
lj_arch.h maps that to LUAJIT_OS_POSIX.

The two are not layout-compatible.  LJ_HASPROFILE is 1 for POSIX and 0 for
OTHER, and it adds three fields to the end of jit_State.  jit_State precedes
the dispatch table inside GG_State, and the assembler VM addresses global state
at offsets from that table which buildvm computed with the host's layout.  So
every such access was 16 bytes off.  The result on QNX aarch64 is a crash in
the very first C call the VM makes -- luaopen_base -> lj_tab_setstr, walking a
hash chain through a corrupted lua_State -- for any script, with or without
the JIT.  It builds and links without a warning.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

diff --git a/src/Makefile b/src/Makefile
index 0b8c04f..b5a1e77 100644
--- a/src/Makefile
+++ b/src/Makefile
@@ -373,12 +373,16 @@ ifneq ($(HOST_SYS),$(TARGET_SYS))
   else
   ifeq (iOS,$(TARGET_SYS))
     HOST_XCFLAGS+= -DLUAJIT_OS=LUAJIT_OS_OSX -DLUAJIT_TARGET_IPHONE=1
+  else
+  ifeq (QNX,$(TARGET_SYS))
+    HOST_XCFLAGS+= -DLUAJIT_OS=LUAJIT_OS_POSIX
   else
     HOST_XCFLAGS+= -DLUAJIT_OS=LUAJIT_OS_OTHER
   endif
   endif
   endif
   endif
+  endif
 endif
 
 ifneq (,$(CCDEBUG))
